.TH FKPT2 1 "November 25, 2026" "fkPT2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fkpt2 \- compute one-loop redshift-space power spectrum multipoles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fkpt2
.RI [ parameter-file ]
.RI [ "name=value ..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fkpt2
computes one-loop redshift-space multipoles from a linear power spectrum.
The default build includes LCDM, Hu\[en]Sawicki f(R), DGP, and massive-neutrino
models and can compute real-space CLPT correlations and Gaussian Streaming
Model multipoles.
.PP
A parameter file accepts
.I "name = value"
or
.IR "name value" .
The characters # and % start comments outside quoted values.
Command-line settings override entries in the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show the parameter list and defaults for the current build.
.TP
.B options=print-models
List the available gravity models.
.TP
.BI fnamePS= path
Read the linear spectrum at
.BR zout .
The first two columns give k in h/Mpc and P(k) in (Mpc/h)\[S3].
.TP
.BI model= name
Select the gravity model. Use
.B model=HS fR0=1e-5
to select F5.
.TP
.B clpt=true
Compute real-space correlations and displacement correlators.
.TP
.B gsm=true
Compute Gaussian Streaming Model multipoles and their CLPT inputs.
.TP
.BI rootDir= directory
Set the output directory. The default is
.BR Output .
.TP
.BI numberThreads= count
Set the thread count for an OpenMP build.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B rsd_multipoles.txt
Wave number and monopole, quadrupole, and hexadecapole of the power spectrum.
.TP
.B tmp/
Resolved parameter values and, when
.B verbose_log=1
is set, a run log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fkpt2 model=HS fR0=1e-5 rootDir=Output_F5
fkpt2 run.ini fR0=1e-6 rootDir=Output_F6
fkpt2 gsm=true
.fi
.PP
With the CLASS addon linked, use a combined
.B [class]
and
.B [fkpt2]
parameter file.
.nf
fkpt2 scripts/class_fkpt2.ini
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The fkPT2 Sphinx manual in docs/index.rst and the project README.
